      "title": "Floor Technician",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\n\nLocation: Jefferson City\n\nPURPOSE: The Floor Technician is responsible for maintaining and restoring hard floor and carpeted surfaces throughout campus facilities. This position performs specialized floor care services including stripping, waxing, buffing, scrubbing, extraction, and preventative maintenance to ensure floors remain clean, safe, and presentable. The Floor Technician supports the overall appearance and cleanliness of campus buildings through scheduled and project-based floor care. ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS, DUTIES, & RESPONSIBILITIES: Floor Care & Maintenance: Strip, wax, seal, burnish, buff, and scrub hard floor surfaces. Shampoo, extract, spot clean, and maintain carpeted areas. Operate auto scrubbers, buffers, burnishers, extractors, and related equipment. Perform routine floor inspections and identify repair or maintenance needs. Maintain entry mats and help reduce dirt and moisture tracking. Project Work: Complete scheduled deep cleaning and floor restoration projects. Support summer turnover, break periods, and special event preparation. Move light furniture or equipment as needed to complete floor care work. Assist with general custodial duties when assigned. Safety & Compliance: Follow proper chemical mixing, handling, and application procedures. Use PPE and safety signage during floor care operations. Maintain equipment in safe working condition and report repair needs. Follow all institutional safety policies and procedures. Customer Service: Work professionally around students, faculty, staff, and visitors. Minimize disruption to building operations while completing assigned work. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS, & ABILITIES: Knowledge of floor care methods, cleaning chemicals, finishes, and surface maintenance procedures. Knowledge of safe work practices, PPE usage, and proper chemical handling procedures. Skill in operating commercial floor equipment such as auto scrubbers, buffers, burnishers, and extractors. Skill in identifying floor care needs and selecting the appropriate cleaning or restoration method. Ability to work independently and complete assignments with minimal supervision. Ability to prioritize tasks and manage time effectively in multiple buildings or work areas. Ability to follow written and verbal instructions accurately. Ability to communicate professionally with supervisors, coworkers, students, faculty, and staff. Ability to maintain consistent attendance and dependable work performance. Ability to adapt to changing schedules, priorities, and operational needs. QUALIFICATIONS: High school diploma or equivalent preferred. Ability to work independently and manage assigned routes/projects. Reliable attendance and strong attention to detail. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Prior floor care, custodial, or environmental services experience. Experience operating commercial floor equipment. Knowledge of floor finishes, coatings, and carpet care methods. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Prolonged standing and walking throughout campus facilities. Ability to lift, carry, push, or pull up to 50 lbs. Frequent bending, stooping, kneeling, and reaching. Ability to push/pull floor equipment and supply carts. Exposure to cleaning chemicals, dust, noise, and varying indoor/outdoor conditions. This job description is not intended to be a complete list of all responsibilities, duties or skills required for the job and is subject to review and change at any time, with or without notice, in accordance with the needs of Lincoln University. Since no job description can detail all the duties and responsibilities that may be required from time to time in the performance of a job, duties and responsibilities that may be inherent in a job, reasonably required for its performance, or required due to the changing nature of the job shall also be considered part of the jobholder's responsibility.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=6105d53b-aeb8-4656-a07d-2743bd4a2423&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9202035558422_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\n\nLocation: Jefferson City\n\nJob Summary: Replacement faculty position in Biology to fill instructional needs. This is a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track position in the STM department. This position will be supporting the Master of Science in Natural Sciences and undergraduate programs including those in Biology, Agriculture, Nursing, Education, and the various pre professional programs on campus.  Essential Job Functions, Duties, & Responsibilities: Full-time, nine-month, tenure-track appointment teaching a full-time load. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in plant biology, general biology, biology for majors, and an active externally funded research program involving undergraduate students.   The ability to teach plant physiology and plant taxonomy is preferred.   Lincoln University faculty are expected to also advise and mentor students and serve on departmental and institutional committees.  Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Curriculum development, mentoring, advising, participating in program assessment, review, and maintaining office hours will be required. Minimum Qualifications: PhD. in Biology, Plant Biology or a related area is required – ABDs considered.  Preferred Qualifications: Post-doctoral experience is a plus. Prior teaching experience is strongly desired. Experience with undergraduate biology-related clubs or organizations. Physical Demands Light sedentary office work. Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer Ability to lift up to 25 lbs. Lincoln University is an Equal Opportunity Employer.  Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and institutional needs. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process should contact the Office of Human Resources at 573-681-5018.",
      "department": ""
