      "title": "Instructor of Mathematics",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\n\nLocation: Jefferson City\n\nJob Summary: The Department of Science, Technology and Mathematics at Lincoln University invites applications for a full time Instructor of Mathematics position. This full-time, nine-month, non-tenure track role is designed for a dedicated educator looking to transition into academia with a focus in mathematics and mathematics education.  Essential Job Functions, Duties, & Responsibilities: Primary teaching areas include lower-division undergraduate mathematics courses. Maintain regular office hours to provide high-quality instructional support to students. Lincoln University faculty are expected to also advise and mentor students and serve on  departmental and institutional committees, as required. All duties pertinent to teaching, including curriculum development, mentoring, advising, participating in program assessment, review, and maintaining office hours will be required. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Personal Characteristics: Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching at the undergraduate level. Experience in various pedagogical teaching techniques in mathematics is a plus. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in mathematics or (a related area) is required. Ability to engage a diverse student body is required. Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching experience (especially of a diverse student body) is strongly desired. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Light sedentary office work. Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer. Ability to lift up to 25 lbs. Lincoln University is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Employment decisions are based on qualifications, merit, and institutional needs. Applicants requiring a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process should contact the Office of Human Resources at 573-681-5018.",
